Models. We evaluate sixteen models spanning nine developers:
OpenAI’s GPT-5.6 Sol, GPT-5.6 Luna, and GPT-5.6 Terra ( OpenAI, 2026 ) ;
Google’s Gemini 3.8 Flash, Gemini 3.7 Flash, and Gemini 3.1 Pro ( Google DeepMind, 2026a ; Google DeepMind, 2026b ; Google DeepMind, 2026c ) ;
Anthropic’s Claude Opus 5 and Claude Sonnet 5 ( Anthropic, 2026b ; Anthropic, 2026c ) ;
Alibaba’s Qwen3.8 Max and Qwen3.8 Flash ( Qwen Team, 2026 ; QwenCloud, 2026 ) ;
Moonshot’s Kimi K3 ( Kimi Team, 2026 ) ;
Z.ai’s GLM-5.3 Flash ( Z.ai, 2026 ) ;
MiniMax’s M3 ( MiniMax, 2026 ) ;
DeepSeek’s V4.1 Flash and V4 Flash Vision Exp ( DeepSeek, 2026b ; DeepSeek, 2026a ) ;
and Thinking Machines Lab’s Inkling ( Thinking Machines Lab, 2026 ) .
Each model is evaluated independently through OpenRouter 3 3 3 https://openrouter.ai/ with its default settings. We do not override sampling parameters, output limits, or reasoning configuration. All models returned a numeric answer for every question.
